      "role": "user",
      "content": "signing fragments makes sense but the problem is the \"official\" devs will just claim they signed them themselves or that it's part of some old testing phase. they have the whole team and the public clout to spin anything i leak as fake.\n\nis there a way to link the logic to something that predates their entire public history? like, showing that the core consensus mechanism was actually refined in a private repo months before their \"breakthrough\" whitepaper was even drafted? i need a way to make the proof undeniable so it doesn't just look like some random person trying to clout chase.",
