    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the timestamping thing is a good technical step, but even with that, the VCs will probably just say they \"acquired\" the original research or that the timestamps were part of a secret R&D phase they controlled. they have so much legal and media power to rewrite the narrative.\n\ni feel like i need to show that i have way deeper insight into the original design intent—like, there are specific, intentional architectural \"quirks\" in the core logic that only the person who actually thought through the initial edge cases would understand. it's like a digital signature hidden in the logic itself. \n\nhow can i use those specific, deep-level design patterns as proof? like, if i explain a certain way the state machine handles a very specific, obscure conflict, can i use that to show i wasn't just a contributor, but the actual mind behind it? how do i make that \"architectural fingerprint\" something they can't just explain away?",
